---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SOURCE } from '../links';

/*
 * Astro writes this to `dist/404.html`. Nothing serves it automatically: the
 * Caddy block for rhizolog.com has to rewrite errors to it, or the site returns
 * Caddy's own bare 404 instead. See `knowledge-base/product-site.md`.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Not found"
  description="Nothing has been written at this address."
  noindex
>
  <section class="flex flex-col items-center px-5 py-20 text-center sm:py-32">
    <svg width="88" height="88" viewBox="0 0 88 88" aria-hidden="true" class="mb-10">
      <circle
        cx="44"
        cy="44"
        r="32"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--color-amber)"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-dasharray="6 7"></circle>
    </svg>

    <p class="mb-5 font-mono text-label tracking-[0.16em] text-mint-dim">404</p>

    <h1
      class="mb-6 max-w-[620px] font-mono text-[27px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink-bright sm:text-h2"
    >
      Nothing has been written here yet.
    </h1>

    <p class="mb-4 max-w-[560px] text-small text-ink-dim sm:text-body">
      Inside a Rhizolog wiki this would not be an error. A link to a page that does not exist is a
      <em class="text-amber not-italic">wanted page</em>: it is drawn on the graph as a dashed ring,
      it shows on the dashboard, and it starts working the moment somebody writes it.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-10 max-w-[560px] text-small text-ink-dim sm:text-body">
      On a website it is just a 404.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5 sm:flex-row sm:gap-3">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="rounded-[3px] bg-mint px-[22px] py-[15px] font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-ground hover:bg-mint-bright sm:py-[13px]"
      >
        Back to the front page
      </a>
      <a
        href={SOURCE}
        class="rounded-[3px] border border-line-strong px-[22px] py-[14px] font-mono text-sm text-ink hover:border-mint-dim sm:py-3"
      >
        Source on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
